WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.699
Why cosine?

00:00:01.699 --> 00:00:04.973
A circle point gives a real Legendre input.

00:00:05.303 --> 00:00:07.908
Mark z on the unit circle at angle t.

00:00:07.908 --> 00:00:11.620
Its reciprocal is its mirror image across the real axis.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.317
Join the two points.

00:00:13.317 --> 00:00:18.266
Their midpoint keeps their common horizontal coordinate, x equals cosine t.

00:00:18.596 --> 00:00:20.383
The midpoint sweeps the interval.

00:00:20.383 --> 00:00:24.036
Turn from zero to pi, sweeping x from one to minus one.

00:00:24.366 --> 00:00:25.925
Stop at ninety degrees.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.335
The input is zero.

00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:31.815
The quadratic Legendre polynomial takes the value minus one half there.

00:00:32.145 --> 00:00:33.420
Read the graph.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.115
The input is zero and the height is minus one half.

